.TH PYTHON 1
.SH NAME
python \- MicroPython, the Python 3 language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python
.br
.B python
.I file
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B python \-c
.IR code ...
.br
.B python \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B python
is MicroPython, the Python 3 language in a small interpreter. Without
arguments it gives the prompt
.RB ( >>>
and
.B ...
lines; Ctrl-D leaves). With a
.IR file ,
it runs that script, with
.B sys.argv
=
.RI [ file ", " args ...].
Ctrl-C raises KeyboardInterrupt.
.PP
Modules:
.BR sys ,
.BR os ,
.BR time ,
.BR math ,
.BR json ,
.BR re ,
.BR struct ,
.BR binascii ,
.BR hashlib ,
.BR random ,
.BR collections ,
.BR heapq ,
.BR errno ,
.BR io ,
.BR array ,
.BR gc ,
.BR micropython ,
.B socket
(TCP and UDP through the network server) and
.B ssl
(TLS 1.3 or 1.2, certificates checked against
.IR /etc/ssl/roots ).
.B os.system
runs
.B sh \-c
and returns its status.
.B import
reads
.B .py
files from the script's folder (or the current one), then
.IR /lib/python .
.PP
The shell splits a command line at spaces and removes double quotes, so
in
.B python \-c
use single quotes for strings. A program's command line has room for 256
bytes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " code"
Run
.IR code :
the words after
.BR \-c ,
joined by spaces.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /lib/python
Modules for
.BR import .
.TP
.I /src/python
Two examples:
.BI primes.py " n"
and
.BI words.py " file" \fR...
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
python /src/python/primes.py 1000
python \-c print('a b', 2**100)
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sh (1),
.BR cc (1)
.SH BUGS
No
.BR signal ,
.BR os.path ,
.BR os.environ ,
.BR subprocess ,
.BR threading ,
.BR select ,
.BR zlib ,
.B datetime
or
.B cmath
modules; no
.B \-m
.IR module ;
no
.B .mpy
files. On AArch64 a 17-digit float literal can be one unit off in the
last place.
